          <p><b>Problem.</b> The relay from sidecar to UI is a shallow pass=
-through chain: every module re-declares the event shape it just received, =
then forwards it. The Rust arm (<span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">sidecar.r=
s:624-683</span>) is stringly-typed: a forgotten match arm drops the event =
with a <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">println!</span>, no compile error.=
 <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">tauri-api.ts:1004</span> still listens f=
or <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">task:update</span>, which nothing emit=
s: an adapter with no behaviour behind it.</p>
          <p><b>Solution.</b> Replace the per-event match with a generic fo=
rwarder (<span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">sidecar:{type}</span>) plus one =
typed side-effect registry for the few events that carry Rust logic (<span =
class=3D"font-mono text-sm">task_complete</span> =E2=86=92 automation compl=
etion). Frontend consumes one typed subscription keyed off the sidecar's <s=
pan class=3D"font-mono text-sm">types.ts</span> union.</p>
          <ul class=3D"text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside text-slate-7=
00">
            <li>Leverage: one interface, every event type</li>
            <li>Locality: new event =3D two edits</li>
            <li>Silent-drop seam becomes type-checked</li>
            <li>Deletes the vestigial <span class=3D"font-mono">task:update=
</span> adapter</li>
            <li>Deletion test passes: rename table adds nothing</li>
          </ul>
