          <p><b>Problem.</b> The "one automation run at a time" invariant i=
s a raw <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">AtomicBool</span> acquired in two=
 places, released in one, and hand-released on four early-return paths. It =
leaks today: <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">run_automation_now</span> di=
spatches without acquiring the slot, yet its completion path calls <span cl=
ass=3D"font-mono text-sm">mark_automation_run_complete</span>, which uncond=
itionally releases (<span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">scheduler:397</span>)=
, so a manual run can free the slot while a scheduled run is mid-flight. Th=
e create-task/create-run/assign/dispatch sequence is also copied verbatim i=
n two files, and the copies have already diverged.</p>
          <p><b>Solution.</b> A <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">DispatchS=
lot</span> module with <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">try_acquire() =E2=
=86=92 Option&lt;Guard&gt;</span>; the Guard releases on drop. Fold both di=
spatch sequences into one <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">dispatch_automa=
tion_run</span> that owns slot handling, so Run Now crosses the same seam.<=
/p>
          <ul class=3D"text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside text-slate-7=
00">
            <li>Locality: concurrency contract in one module</li>
            <li>Release-leak becomes structurally impossible</li>
            <li>Leverage: two callers, one implementation</li>
            <li>Slot testable without threads or DB</li>
            <li>Closes a live correctness bug</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

