>cron</span> crate is 1-indexed Sunday-first; Unix is 0-indexed) and <span =
class=3D"font-mono text-sm">compute_next_fire</span> are pure, yet live as =
private methods on <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">AutomationSchedulerReg=
istry</span>. The <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">normalize_cron_public</=
span> escape hatch exists only because <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">va=
lidate_cron</span> wanted the behaviour without the registry: the tell that=
