          <p><b>Problem.</b> Startup repo sync is ~105 lines inline in the =
<span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">.setup()</span> closure, a near-verbatim =
copy of the <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">skill_repos_sync</span> comma=
nd, differing only in lock recovery. The leaf modules underneath (<span cla=
ss=3D"font-mono text-sm">git_ops</span>: 12 tests) are deep; the orchestrat=
ion above them has no function boundary, needs an <span class=3D"font-mono =
text-sm">AppHandle</span>, and has zero tests. Deletion test fails for the =
pair: removing the <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">lib.rs</span> block le=
aves the command fully working: proof they are copy-paste, not one module.<=
/p>
          <p><b>Solution.</b> Extract <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">fn =
sync_repo(conn, cache_dir, repo, token) =E2=86=92 Result&lt;Vec&lt;StoredRe=
poSkill&gt;&gt;</span>. Both callers invoke it; <span class=3D"font-mono te=
xt-sm">AppHandle</span> and event emission stay at the edges. Unit-test wit=
h a tempdir and a local git origin.</p>
          <ul class=3D"text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside text-slate-7=
00">
            <li>Deletes ~100 duplicated lines</li>
            <li>Sync algorithm becomes unit-testable</li>
            <li>Locality: one place for sync bugs</li>
            <li>Deep leaves gain a deep orchestrator</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

