          <p><b>Problem.</b> Rust infers a category by prefix-matching the =
skill id, persists it, ships it to the UI, where the grid re-derives by key=
word-matching the skill name and uses the Rust value only as a third-priori=
ty fallback. Two taxonomies (12 vs 13 categories, <span class=3D"font-mono =
text-sm">Development</span> exists only in TS). Deletion test: stub the Rus=
t branches to <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">"General"</span> and the gr=
id barely changes: the Rust computation carries almost no leverage, yet eve=
ry scan path pays for it.</p>
          <p><b>Solution.</b> Pick one owner. Simplest: ship raw <span clas=
s=3D"font-mono text-sm">id</span> + <span class=3D"font-mono text-sm">name<=
/span> and let the TS taxonomy decide; delete the Rust inference. (Or move =
the keyword rule into Rust and have the UI trust <span class=3D"font-mono t=
ext-sm">skill.category</span>.)</p>
          <ul class=3D"text-sm space-y-1 list-disc list-inside text-slate-7=
00">
            <li>Badge predictable from one interface</li>
            <li>One taxonomy to extend</li>
            <li>Deletes a no-leverage computation</li>
